{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 51,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hearken to me, ye that follow after righteousness, ye that seek the LORD: look to the rock ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whence",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye are hewn, and to the hole of the pit ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whence",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye are digged.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Look to Abraham your father, and to Sarah ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bore you: for I called him alone, and blessed him, and increased him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the LORD will comfort Zion: he will comfort all her waste places; and he will make her wilderness like Eden, and her desert like the garden of the LORD; joy and gladness shall be found therein, thanksgiving, and the voice of melody.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hearken to me, my people; and give ear to me, O my nation: for a law shall proceed from me, and I will make my judgment to rest for a light of the people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My righteousness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " near; my salvation is gone forth, and my arms shall judge the people; the isles shall wait upon me, and on my arm shall they trust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lift up your eyes to the heavens, and look upon the earth beneath: for the heavens shall vanish away like smoke, and the earth shall become old like a garment, and its inhabitants shall die in like manner: but my salvation shall be for ever, and my righteousness shall not be abolished.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hearken to me, ye that know righteousness, the people in whose heart ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my law; fear ye not the reproach of men, neither be ye afraid of their revilings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the moth shall eat them like a garment, and the worm shall eat them like wool: but my righteousness shall be for ever, and my salvation from generation to generation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Awake, awake, put on thy strength, O arm of the LORD; awake, as in the ancient days, in the generations of old. ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou not that which hath cut Rahab, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wounded the dragon?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou not that which hath dried the sea, the waters of the great deep; that hath made the depths of the sea a way for the ransomed to pass over?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore the redeemed of the LORD shall return, and come with singing to Zion; and everlasting joy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon their head: they shall obtain gladness and joy; sorrow and mourning shall flee away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that comforteth you: who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou, that thou shouldest be afraid of a man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall die, and of the son of man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall be made ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " grass;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And forgettest the LORD thy maker, that hath stretched forth the heavens, and laid the foundations of the earth; and hast feared continually every day because of the fury of the oppressor, as if he were ready to destroy? and where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the fury of the oppressor?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The captive exile hasteneth that he may be loosed, and that he should not die in the pit, nor that his bread should fail.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD thy God, that divided the sea, whose waves roared: The LORD of hosts ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I have put my words in thy mouth, and have covered thee in the shade of my hand, that I may plant the heavens, and lay the foundations of the earth, and say to Zion, Thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Awake, awake, stand up, O Jerusalem, which hast drank at the hand of the LORD the cup of his fury; thou hast drank the dregs of the cup of trembling, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wrung ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none to guide her among all the sons ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whom",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " she hath brought forth; neither ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is there any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that taketh her by the hand of all the sons ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " she hath brought up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These two ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " have come to thee; who shall be sorry for thee? desolation, and destruction, and famine, and the sword: by whom shall I comfort thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy sons have fainted, they lie at the head of all the streets, as a wild bull in a net: they are full of the fury of the LORD, the rebuke of thy God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore hear now this, thou afflicted, and drunken, but not with wine:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith thy Lord Jehovah, and thy God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pleadeth the cause of his people, Behold, I have taken out of thy hand the cup of trembling, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the dregs of the cup of my fury; thou shalt no more drink it again:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.51.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.51.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I will put it into the hand of them that afflict thee; who have said to thy soul, Prostrate thyself, that we may go over: and thou hast laid thy body as the ground, and as the street, to them that went over.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
